      "writtenOn": "2023-04-19T18:10:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that sounds like a result of alias analysis. \n\n\u003e OTOH, doing the little dance of defining data_end seems to confuse the compiler enough that it doesn\u0027t optimize out the comparison.\n\nThe pesky devs have a habit of making the compilers smarter over time, so that\u0027s typically not a great long-term strategy.\n\nMaybe there is a correct way how to do this in Rust, but I wouldn\u0027t be opposed to a small asm macro like we have for sysregs, or a C file, basically a language that doesn\u0027t make that non-alias assumption.",
      "parentUuid": "31165cec_8626186b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 275,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 275,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "2b00fa542cd9ca75d4b9077d271d107cb522f8dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
