      "lineNbr": 316,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T10:20:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is all a bit vague, so it\u0027s hard to know exactly what you\u0027re trying to do here.\n\nThe architecture doesn\u0027t require explicit synchronisation to order a prior indirect system register read against a later direct write, so I\u0027m inclined to say that neither the `DSB NSH` nor the following `ISB` are necessary when the MMU is being disabled. The thing to ensure is that the cache maintenance has completed before entering the payload, and the `DSB` right before the indirect branch should take care of that. I don\u0027t understand why you zero the `TTBR` nor why that\u0027s followed up with an `ISB`.",
      "parentUuid": "1ef6accb_75933146",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 316,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 316,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "2b00fa542cd9ca75d4b9077d271d107cb522f8dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
