      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T10:53:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The architecture doesn\u0027t require explicit synchronisation to order a prior indirect system register read against a later direct write\n\nThanks for confirming!\n\n\u003e neither the `DSB NSH` nor the following `ISB` are necessary\n\nRemoved.\n\n\u003e The thing to ensure is that the cache maintenance has completed before entering the payload\n\nAdded a comment to the `DSB` with this info.\n\n\u003e  I don\u0027t understand why you zero the `TTBR` ...\n\nThe idea was to put the pVM/vCPU back in a state that is as close as possible to its state out of reset but it\u0027s not intended to have any other effect.\n\n\u003e ... nor why that\u0027s followed up with an `ISB`.\n\nIt looks like a [review comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2090005/comment/cac0c58f_db744676/) referring to [the `ISB` above](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2090005/comment/5c0ee5c3_fa3ec938/) was misinterpreted? I\u0027ve removed it.",
      "parentUuid": "2b9061b1_90c333f7",
